A||||5||GWMORGAN||REPLACING VACUUM LINES.||||1
Z||000000||GWMORGAN||10-08-1999||08:39 PM||||How hard/easy is it to replace the entire vacuum lines? Do I have to remove the plenum*  (*sp*?) to accomplish this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||10-08-1999||10:42 PM||||actually no,remove all the lines, then your car has a diagram, on how it's all connected.buy the hoses and carefully put them in under the plenum,it takes a little time to do it but it can be done.also a little helpfull tip, when taking off the old factory lines,snap them before the little connections, that way you can buy one only one size and you can connect them into those hoses, like the ones  under the plenum, use the same connection just snap it of so you can connect the new line in it.i did mine in maybe an hour going slow, also the line to the pressure fuel regulator snap it off a liitle bit more, because if you take it all off it is hard to reconnect that line with the plenum off. well i hope you understood what i told you and good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||10-09-1999||03:18 AM||||AL,<BR>  Thanks for info.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||10-09-1999||05:57 AM||||Would anyone know where one can get a new set of vacuum lines for the 2.8v6? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steven||10-09-1999||09:25 PM||||Hate to give you the bad news. I work at GM Service Parts Operations, and I know that the plastic vac. lines that are under the plenum are discon. I have a copy of the prints and am will to send them to you by mail. I have the same problem and am planning to use steel brake line and bend them to OEM specs. on my engine rebuild over the winter. You will have to let me know. E-mail me at p_car_guy@yahoo.com and let me know.<p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 10-09-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||AL||10-10-1999||04:35 AM||||the vacuam lines i have, were bought at autozone.i bought 5/32 in size and it worked perfectly, plus you don't have to worry about the hoses snapping, like in the original lines that the car came with. the foot cost 35 cents so buy at least 12 feet i hoses to be on the safe side, good luck guys.||||reg||6
